crisis over ukraine us allies are  negotiating for peace and preparing for  a possible war french president emmanuel  macron met with ukraine's president  yesterday and said the standoff with  russia could go on for weeks and months  at the same time nato forces hoping to  encourage russia not to invade ukraine  holding a series of war games in nearby  estonia and charlie dagetta is there  british and estonian tanks square off  against each other in a snowy wasteland  not far from the russian border  nato partners locked in a simulated  battle  with the massive russian military  escalation near ukraine sending jitters  throughout this entire region  these war games have never been more  real  if a conflict were to break out in this  region these are exactly the conditions  they'd be dealing with deep snow a  difficult terrain limited visibility  against an enemy that far outnumbers  these forces in terms of troops and  weaponry  the baltic states lie right along the  borders of russia and belarus each home  to a multinational nato battle group  american reinforcements have been  deployed to poland and romania  while moscow has sent tens of thousands  of forces to belarus part of a massive  russian military buildup  there are still hopes for a diplomatic  solution to the crisis in ukraine  but military preparations are never  based on a best-case scenario  for cbs mornings charlie dagetta lasna  estonia
 

